ue] [17592186335054 1089 "q-149727" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335054 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535167 true] [17592186335054 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057794/assets/8d060e257d74e6e0e6b7f35bfb89e9e974499059ddf4d029c0cace195ba67c13.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}\\frac{1}{y-x}\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the segment of the line $x=2y-4$ from $(0,2)$ to $(2,3),$ as shown above." 13194139535167 true] [17592186335054 1113 #uuid "d191f591-a7c2-57bc-932c-5a5f3f087d67" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335054 1145 "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2t-4.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2t-4,\\,t⟩,\\,2\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $2\\le t\\le 3$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-4)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y-x},$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{t-(2t-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{1}{y-x}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{4-t}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{4-t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=4-t,$ $\\text{d}u=-\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{4-t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{2}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{2}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡u]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335056 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335057 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335058 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335059 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335060 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1041 "selection" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335059 13194139535167 true] [17592186335055 1110 #uuid "668caa80-98a9-502f-85ca-39013fb9c0b7" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335056 1034 "2\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335056 1111 #uuid "da29604b-c306-5f14-b00c-f21e120b7224" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335057 1034 "4\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335057 1111 #uuid "7e845026-062c-57db-a527-5dbd1d0a8cf7" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335058 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335058 1111 #uuid "43e6280f-4b51-53c1-9328-bf7ee068ed24" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335059 1034 "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335059 1111 #uuid "03f3d8c0-91bc-5783-8351-f00328ea4fdc" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335060 1034 "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335060 1111 #uuid "2f0913eb-328a-51d9-a452-2bd0ae217e29" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335061 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335062 13194139535167 true] [17592186335061 1089 "q-149745" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335061 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535167 true] [17592186335061 1100 "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}6{x}^{6}{e}^{-2y}\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x={e}^{y/2}$ from $(1,0)$ to $(\\sqrt{2},\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).$" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335061 1113 #uuid "35b5f79b-1789-56ee-87fc-9d9e17bf906f" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335061 1145 "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)={e}^{t/2}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{e}^{t/2},\\,t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $0\\le t\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t/2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{2}\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{2})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{e}^{t}}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=6{x}^{6}{e}^{-2y}$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =6{x}^{6}{e}^{-2y} \\\\  & =6{({e}^{t/2})}^{6}{e}^{-2t} \\\\  & =6{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}6{x}^{6}{e}^{-2y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}6{e}^{t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+4}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u={e}^{t}+4,$ $\\text{d}u={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{5}^{6}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{5}^{6} \\\\  & =2({6}^{3/2}-{5}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =2(6\\sqrt{6}-5\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{6}-10\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335063 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335064 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335065 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335066 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335067 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1041 "selection" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335067 13194139535167 true] [17592186335062 1110 #uuid "3dbf2235-81e5-5e46-9ee4-bc40647be362" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335063 1034 "5\\sqrt{6}-6\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335063 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335063 1111 #uuid "7be731cd-1503-5c9c-9db7-366a599e493c" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335064 1034 "\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335064 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335064 1111 #uuid "165d80bc-691d-532b-8f3b-e1ea11737379" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335065 1034 "6\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535167 true] [17592186335065 1111 #uuid "89d95ab6-b087-5940-93f5-230ae06de0d2" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335066 1034 "2\\sqrt{6}-5\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535167 true] [17592186335066 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13